node_modules

# Build output. `just build` makes it; `npm pack` publishes dist/flow.mjs (the binary),
# dist/index.mjs (the grammar), dist/packs.mjs (the ten packs) and dist/types/ from the
# working tree. Committing bundles plus their sourcemaps would put generated artefacts in
# every diff for no reader's benefit.
dist/

# Working-docs journal — a symlink into ~/.work/journals/flow. No trailing slash, so a folder
# OR a stray symlink named .work is always ignored and never committed.
.work

# Per-worktree active-task marker, written by `work start`
.work-current

# Per-machine agent settings — never commit (permission grants etc.)
.claude/settings.local.json

# The guard's own state (the event log, the session marker, the off switch, the recorder) lives
# at `.flow/`, a real directory at the repo root. There is deliberately nothing to add here for
# it: `.flow/` writes a self-ignoring .gitignore of its own, so it can never be committed and
# this file never has to know it exists.
#
# What a guarded repo DOES commit is `flow.config.ts`, any pack it writes itself under `guards/`,
# and `.githooks/pre-commit`. That is the whole guard: the packs this package ships arrive with
# the install, there is no rule library anywhere on the machine, and nothing resolves at run time.

# Provisioned by the secrets pack — the three files that must never be committed.
.env.keys

# Provisioned by the secrets pack — the three files that must never be committed.
.dev.vars

# Provisioned by the secrets pack — the three files that must never be committed.
.env.*.local

# This worktree's dev port, written fresh by the worktrunk pre-start hook.
.wt-port
